WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:02.990
Technological quirks look
very much like the

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:05.180
traditional stoppers
that are cut and shaped

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.230
from a solid piece of
cork.

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:10.100
These two are made of
natural cork, only very

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.270
differently. Cork is the
bark of the cork oak

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:18.440
tree. Once the tree
reaches the age of 25, it

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.760
can be harvested for its
bark.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:21.920
Once every decade or so.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:25.100
A specialized worker
makes cuts in the bark

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.190
with an axe, using a
very specific technique

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.240
that doesn't harm the
tree.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.740
Using the handle of the
axe, he gently pries off

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:37.640
the bark. A cork oak
typically lives for 300

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:41.240
years and can be
harvested up to 15 times.

